{# Prompt text the `screenshot` tool returns beside the image. One block per call
   form; each is rendered on its own, never together. #}
{% block draft_review %}REVIEW THIS DRAFT — the user has NOT seen it.
· Look at the image. Blank, empty, or just a bare axes/frame with nothing plotted? That means the code ran but rendered nothing (e.g. a matplotlib script ending in `plt.show()` instead of the figure) — fix the code so it actually produces output, then call `screenshot(code=...)` again. Do not say it looks good without seeing content.
· Wrong, ugly, cluttered, or missing something? → fix it and look again. For a small change — a colour, a title, one line — call `edit(snippet_id, old_str, new_str)` with the draft id below, then `screenshot(draft_id=...)`, rather than resending the whole snippet with `screenshot(code=...)`. You are still reviewing here, so looking again is the point.
· Looks right AND shows real content? → call `show(draft_id=...)` once, using the draft id given below, to hand it to the user. Do NOT resend the code — the draft has already been rendered and checked, so promoting it is free and guarantees the user gets exactly what you just looked at.
· A CONTROLS or BELOW THE FOLD note above? You are looking at part of this draft. Judge only what you can see, and re-capture with `full_page=True` or `do=[{"click": "<name>"}]` before calling the whole thing finished.
Do not describe this draft or its problems to the user; just iterate until it is right.{% endblock %}
{% block shown_image %}IMAGE QUALITY CHECK — before answering:
· Blurry, pixelated, or clipped? → answer from the code/data instead.
· Text/labels too small to read confidently? → answer from the code/data instead.
· Image is clear and complete? → answer from THIS image only. Do NOT recompute from raw data — rendered output and raw data frequently disagree (row order, axis inversion, sorting, binning).
· A CONTROLS or BELOW THE FOLD note above? → this image is part of the visualization, not all of it. Never answer "there is no such thing" about something you have not looked at: re-capture with `do=[{"click": "<name>"}]` or `full_page=True` first. Ask for what the question needs, not for everything.
· Asked to CHANGE it rather than describe it? → `edit(snippet_id, old_str, new_str)` forks it into a new draft, runs it, and returns the new id; pass that straight to `show(draft_id=...)`. Do not resend the whole snippet for a small change, and do not screenshot in between unless you need to see the change.{% endblock %}
